le parameters: 82,202,446 Non-trainable parameters: 0"}]},"footnotes":[],"label":"table","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":457.1183166503906,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":38.19987869262695,"r":573.5614013671875,"t":545.3146514892578},"charspan":[0,0],"page_no":1}],"references":[],"self_ref":"#/tables/2"}],"texts":[{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_header","orig":"(IJACSA) International Journal of Advanced Computer Science and Applications; 1, 2023","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":748.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":271.0,"r":569.3333333333334,"t":769.3333333333334},"charspan":[0,85],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/0","text":"(IJACSA) International Journal of Advanced Computer Science and Applications; 1, 2023"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"THE PERFORMANCE OF THE PROPOSED METHOD FOR DETECTING WHOLE MULTIMODAL VIDEO DEEPFAKES COMPARED TO RECENT STATE-OF-THE ART METHODS ON THE FAKEAVCELEB DATASET","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":694.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":92.66666666666667,"r":568.0,"t":711.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,156],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"THE PERFORMANCE OF THE PROPOSED METHOD FOR DETECTING WHOLE MULTIMODAL VIDEO DEEPFAKES COMPARED TO RECENT STATE-OF-THE ART METHODS ON THE FAKEAVCELEB DATASET"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"TABLE IV. THE GRU-BASED ATTENTION MECHANISM LAYERS DETAILS","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":550.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":182.66666666666666,"r":430.0,"t":559.3333333333334},"charspan":[0,58],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"TABLE IV. THE GRU-BASED ATTENTION MECHANISM LAYERS DETAILS"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The cross-entropy loss (l) function is utilized to measure the   efficiency of the   suggested   deepfake video detection method on three levels: video frames, audio, and the whole video. Its formula [59] is defined as follows:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":405.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":43.0,"r":298.3333333333333,"t":451.3333333333333},"charspan":[0,227],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"The cross-entropy loss (l) function is utilized to measure the   efficiency of the   suggested   deepfake video detection method on three levels: video frames, audio, and the whole video. Its formula [59] is defined as follows:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"1 = M ZM1(yk log(pk) + (1 - yk) log(1 pk)) (20)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":383.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":69.33333333333333,"r":297.6666666666667,"t":399.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,47],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"where M refers to the number of visual videos, audios, or whole videos. The yk and pk denote the actual label and predicted probability corresponding to the kth video. It can be seen in Table III that the proposed method, which represents experiment 3, for whole multimodal video deepfake detection has achieved 97.52% accuracy and 97.21% AUROC. Its performance exceeds that of experiment 2 because experiment 2 is unable to learn intercorrelations between different modalities.  Additionally, it outperforms recent state-of-the-art methods by an average growth of 34.4% accuracy and 34.2% AUROC as can be seen in Table III.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":257.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":42.333333333333336,"r":298.3333333333333,"t":379.0},"charspan":[0,624],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"where M refers to the number of visual videos, audios, or whole videos. The yk and pk denote the actual label and predicted probability corresponding to the kth video. It can be seen in Table III that the proposed method, which represents experiment 3, for whole multimodal video deepfake detection has achieved 97.52% accuracy and 97.21% AUROC. Its performance exceeds that of experiment 2 because experiment 2 is unable to learn intercorrelations between different modalities.  Additionally, it outperforms recent state-of-the-art methods by an average growth of 34.4% accuracy and 34.2% AUROC as can be seen in Table III."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The experiments are carried out using an OMEN HP with 16-gigabyte Intel (R) Core (TM) i7-975OH CPU, a 6gigabyte RTX 2060 GPU, and Windows 11. The  proposed method is implemented the Python programming language.  Python libraries such as Keras, OpenCV, Random; Tensorflow, Numpy; OS, and Librosa are used  during   the implementation. laptop using","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":173.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":42.333333333333336,"r":298.3333333333333,"t":252.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,346],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"The experiments are carried out using an OMEN HP with 16-gigabyte Intel (R) Core (TM) i7-975OH CPU, a 6gigabyte RTX 2060 GPU, and Windows 11. The  proposed method is implemented the Python programming language.  Python libraries such as Keras, OpenCV, Random; Tensorflow, Numpy; OS, and Librosa are used  during   the implementation. laptop using"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The accuracy and loss curves of the proposed method on the training and validation subsets of the FakeAVCeleb dataset for the and whole multimodal   videos, are shown in 7 . Additionally,   the proposed method confusion matrix for deepfake video detection on the three levels is depicted in Fig: 8. Furthermore; 9 shows the receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve Fig Fig;","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":89.37951547596231,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":42.333333333333336,"r":298.3333333333333,"t":169.0},"charspan":[0,378],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"The accuracy and loss curves of the proposed method on the training and validation subsets of the FakeAVCeleb dataset for the and whole multimodal   videos, are shown in 7 . Additionally,   the proposed method confusion matrix for deepfake video detection on the three levels is depicted in Fig: 8. Furthermore; 9 shows the receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve Fig Fig;"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"and the AUROC curve of the proposed method performance. As shown in Fig: 9, the ROC curve is extremely close to the top left ensuring the high performance of the proposed method.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":421.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":313.6666666666667,"r":569.0,"t":458.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,178],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"and the AUROC curve of the proposed method performance. As shown in Fig: 9, the ROC curve is extremely close to the top left ensuring the high performance of the proposed method."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"10 provides comparison of the proposed method with contemporary state-of-the-art methods evaluation metrics. As shown in Fig: 10, the proposed method has yielded better performance in comparison to the other methods on the three levels. It has precision of 96.91%, recall of 100%, FI score of 98.43%, and specificity of 97.22% for detecting visual videos_ Additionally, it has precision of 100%, recall of 95.10%, Fl-score of 97.49%, and specificity of 100% for detecting audios. Further; it has a precision of 98.43%, recall of 97.66%, Fl-score of 98.04%, and specificity of 97.30% for detecting whole multimodal videos. Fig; using","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":295.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":314.0,"r":570.3333333333334,"t":419.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,632],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"10 provides comparison of the proposed method with contemporary state-of-the-art methods evaluation metrics. As shown in Fig: 10, the proposed method has yielded better performance in comparison to the other methods on the three levels. It has precision of 96.91%, recall of 100%, FI score of 98.43%, and specificity of 97.22% for detecting visual videos_ Additionally, it has precision of 100%, recall of 95.10%, Fl-score of 97.49%, and specificity of 100% for detecting audios. Further; it has a precision of 98.43%, recall of 97.66%, Fl-score of 98.04%, and specificity of 97.30% for detecting whole multimodal videos. Fig; using"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"It can be concluded that the proposed upgraded XceptionNet generated useful hierarchical representation of   faces, which   contributed to distinguishing between genuine and fake videos. As well, the proposed CQT based modified InceptionResNetV2 produced valuable time-frequency representation of audio. This assisted to reveal deepfake videos and improved the detection method's effectiveness.  Moreover, a concatenate that is applied to the features extracted from visual video and audio modalities produced an informative bimodal representation of videos. In addition; the GRU-based attention mechanism; which is applied to the visual   video, audio, and bimodal features assisted in capturing the most important temporal information of videos. This in turn helped to detect the   deepfakes. Furthermore, it can be inferred that correlating features from different   modalities can improve   the chances   of  achieving accurate deepfake video detection:. spatial deep layer","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":104.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":313.3333333333333,"r":570.0,"t":294.0},"charspan":[0,977],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"It can be concluded that the proposed upgraded XceptionNet generated useful hierarchical representation of   faces, which   contributed to distinguishing between genuine and fake videos. As well, the proposed CQT based modified InceptionResNetV2 produced valuable time-frequency representation of audio. This assisted to reveal deepfake videos and improved the detection method's effectiveness.  Moreover, a concatenate that is applied to the features extracted from visual video and audio modalities produced an informative bimodal representation of videos. In addition; the GRU-based attention mechanism; which is applied to the visual   video, audio, and bimodal features assisted in capturing the most important temporal information of videos. This in turn helped to detect the   deepfakes. Furthermore, it can be inferred that correlating features from different   modalities can improve   the chances   of  achieving accurate deepfake video detection:. spatial deep layer"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"www ijacsa.thesaiorg","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":18.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":261.0,"r":352.6666666666667,"t":32.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,20],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/11","text":"www ijacsa.thesaiorg"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"416 |P a g e","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":29.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":512.3333333333334,"r":566.3333333333334,"t":44.0},"charspan":[0,12],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/12","text":"416 |P a g e"}],"version":"1.10.0"}